// Hand-written. farming.constant is generated by tools/farming/gen.py, so anything added there is
// lost on the next regeneration; these are not part of the crop table and live here.

// AUTOWEED. Past this Farming level, empty patches stop going back to weeds and any weeds already
// on one are gone the next time the patch is looked at - see ~farming_regrow_weeds in
// farming_core.rs2.
//
// 65 is Corey's own number ("could lock it behind a lvl/xp req like 65 or 70 farming"). There is
// nothing to copy it from: auto-weeding is an RS3 feature, not an Old School one, so this is a
// chosen number rather than a sourced one. 65 is also where the Farming Guild's middle tier opens
// in Old School, which is the closest thing to a precedent there is.
^farming_autoweed_level = 65

// THE AMULET OF NATURE'S YIELD BONUS. Corey's call, 12 October, after the amulet shipped without
// one: "add the yield bonus to the amulet of nature". He asked for 2-5%.
//
// 3% RATHER THAN 5%, and the reason is the Farming cape. The cape pays +5% and costs 99 Farming;
// this amulet costs 27 Magic and some magic roots, so it cannot be worth the same. 3% is the
// middle of the range asked for and sits below the cape, which is the only ordering here that
// makes sense.
//
// IT IS +3% TO CHANCE-TO-SAVE, not +3% to the number of herbs, and that is how the other two
// bonuses in ~farming_cts are defined too: the magic secateurs' published "+10%" is 11/10 on the
// cts roll and the cape's "+5%" is 21/20 on it. Yield follows from cts, but not linearly, so a
// player will not count 3% more herbs - they will fail a save slightly less often.
//
// To change it, change these two numbers and nothing else: 102/100 for 2%, 105/100 for 5%.
^farming_nature_amulet_num = 103
^farming_nature_amulet_div = 100
